This post will get hands on implementing the theme toggle for a SPA using Tanstack Router with TailwindCSS+Shadcn for styling. It's helpful to take a look at a timeline of events comparing between a SPA, SSR, and SSG site. Note some key milestones such as FCP, LCP, and TTI.

![Loading Waterfall](/posts/p/theme-toggle/waterfall.light.png) {% class="block dark:hidden" %}

![Loading Waterfall](/posts/p/theme-toggle/waterfall.dark.png) {% class="hidden dark:block" %}

From this waterfall we can see for a SPA, there are two renders that are important for preventing [Flash of Unstyled Content FOUC](https://webkit.org/blog/66/the-fouc-problem/): rendering the application shell and rendering the hydrated application.

## Rendering the Application Shell

When a SPA is requested from a server first an HTML shell is sent back. This is just an HTML document with a mostly blank `<body>`, however the `<head>` will have links to the resources your application needs.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <meta name="description" content="The personal site for Spencer Duball." />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/logo192.png" />
    <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/src/styles.css" />
    <title>Spencer Duball</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="app"></div>
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.tsx"></script>
  </body>
</html>
```

We know from the [Critical Rendering Path](/posts/p/theme-toggle-spa-ssr-ssg-5c5a2763#critical-rendering-path) that three steps will run in parallel:
- Build DOM Tree
- Preload Parser
- Build CSSOM Tree

The preload parser will make requests for all linked resources as the DOM is parsed. Since the `script` is `type="module"` it will be non-blocking, and before the CSSOM Tree can be build the `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/src/styles.css" />` must be downloaded.

After both the DOM Tree and CSSOM Tree finish being built, a blank shell will render with all of the styles from the `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/src/styles.css" />`. Since we are using shadcn there is typically a style that sets the background color based upon the theme. We need to remove this from the stylesheet and add this class dynamically later!

```diff
@layer base {
  ...
  body {
-   @apply font-sans text-foreground bg-background;
+   @apply font-sans text-foreground;
  }
  ...
}
```

Below is an example where the system (OS) theme is set to dark, the `bg-background` class is added back to the `styles.css`, and the network is throttled to 3G speeds. We can see that the background color flashes white for the initial shell render.

